input_prompt: Explain what on-device AI means in simple terms.

Here's a simple, everyday explanation of "on-device AI":

> Imagine you're using your phone to search for photos, translate text, or get voice commands (like "Hey Siri" or "OK Google") without needing to connect to the internet.  
>   
> On-device AI means that the AI (the smart software that understands language, images, voices, etc.) runs directly on your device—like your phone, tablet, or smart speaker—instead of sending your data to a remote server or cloud.  
>   
> Why is that useful?  
> • **Privacy:** Your photos, voice recordings, or text don’t leave your device. Only you see or control them.  
> • **Speed & reliability:** It works instantly, even without Wi-Fi or internet, because it processes everything locally.  
> • **No data needed:** You don’t have to upload or share your data to get the AI to work.  
>   
> In short: "On-device AI" = the AI works right on your device, keeping things private, fast, and working offline.

It’s like having a tiny, built-in "assistant" inside your phone that handles language, images, or voice without needing to send anything out. Simple, clear, and focused on what matters to you

